xecutions/20260507T030529-d3ec7c21/` (the per-attempt evidence directory under `.ddx/executions/`). **Never write reports to `/tmp` or any path outside the repository** — out-of-repo paths are invisible to the post-merge reviewer and cause BLOCK on missing evidence. If the bead names a specific in-repo path, use it; else default to `.ddx/executions/20260507T030529-d3ec7c21/\u0026lt;short-name\u0026gt;.md`. Stage and commit the report alongside code.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Bead overrides project defaults\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;The bead description and AC override CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, and conservative project defaults (YAGNI, DOWITYTD, no-docs-unless-asked) in this worktree — write whatever the bead asks for.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Review gate\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- The review is a gate, not an escape hatch — meet every AC in this pass.\u0026#xA;- Address every BLOCKING `\u0026lt;review-findings\u0026gt;` item; do not declare `no_changes` with blocking findings open.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Constraints\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Work only inside this execution worktree.\u0026#xA;- Keep `.ddx/executions/` intact — DDx uses it as execution evidence.\u0026#xA;- **Never run `ddx init`** — the workspace is initialized; running it corrupts the bead queue.\u0026#xA;- Do not modify files outside the bead\u0026#39;s named scope.\u0026#xA;- Do not rewrite CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, or other project-instructions files unless the bead asks.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## When the work is done\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;After the commit succeeds and every AC is verified, stop. Return control to the orchestrator — do not keep exploring or testing.\n  \u003c/instructions\u003e\n  \u003cbead id=\"fizeau-9ff62c35\"\u003e\n    \u003ctitle\u003eReplace medium TerminalBench profiles with fiz wrapper lanes for all harnesses\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cdescription\u003e\nThe medium TerminalBench comparison should compare targets by changing fiz routing pins, not by switching Harbor installed agents. The official lanes are fiz-wrapped Claude Sonnet 4.6, fiz-wrapped Codex GPT 5.4 mini, fiz-wrapped pi GPT 5.4 mini, fiz-wrapped opencode GPT 5.4 mini, fiz via OpenRouter Sonnet 4.6, and fiz via OpenRouter GPT 5.4 mini. Raw Harbor Claude/Codex/pi/opencode lanes may remain as diagnostics outside this official script, but they must not be part of the main comparison path.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;In-scope files:\u0026#xA;- scripts/benchmark/run_medium_model_terminalbench_comparison.sh\u0026#xA;- benchmark profile or manifest files used by that script\u0026#xA;- focused shell/profile tests or dry-run checks\u0026#xA;- docs referenced directly by the script if needed\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Out-of-scope:\u0026#xA;- FizeauAgent implementation\u0026#xA;- CLI/service harness pin support\u0026#xA;- result aggregation logic\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Implementation notes:\u0026#xA;- The official script should invoke Harbor with only the `fiz` installed agent/harness.\u0026#xA;- Use lane labels from the spec: `fiz-harness-claude-sonnet-4-6`, `fiz-harness-codex-gpt-5-4-mini`, `fiz-harness-pi-gpt-5-4-mini`, `fiz-harness-opencode-gpt-5-4-mini`, `fiz-openrouter-claude-sonnet-4-6`, and `fiz-openrouter-gpt-5-4-mini`.\u0026#xA;- Default local TerminalBench task image behavior to native builds with `HARBOR_FORCE_BUILD=1` unless explicitly overridden.\n    \u003c/description\u003e\n    \u003cacceptance\u003e\n1. A dry-run/test proves the official medium comparison script passes only the fiz Harbor adapter/installed-agent to Harbor.\u0026#xA;2. The generated profile matrix contains exactly the six official lane labels listed in the spec for the medium frontier comparison.\u0026#xA;3. The script defaults `HARBOR_FORCE_BUILD=1` for local native task-image builds while allowing an explicit user override.\u0026#xA;4. `bash -n scripts/benchmark/run_medium_model_terminalbench_comparison.sh` passes.\u0026#xA;5. Any profile-generation tests for scripts/benchmark pass.\n    \u003c/acceptance\u003e\n    \u003clabels\u003earea:benchmark, area:profiles, kind:task, phase:build\u003c/labels\u003e\n    \u003cmetadata parent=\"fizeau-ed924ab3\" spec-id=\"terminalbench-fiz-wrapper-comparison-2026-05-06\" base-rev=\"c74ff88355fb252cb99538af919baf671bc82465\" bundle=\".ddx/executions/20260507T030529-d3ec7c21\"/\u003e\n  \u003c/bead\u003e\n  \u003cgoverning\u003e\n    \u003cref id=\"terminalbench-fiz-wrapper-comparison-2026-05-06\" path=\"docs/helix/02-design/terminalbench-fiz-wrapper-comparison-2026-05-06.md\"\u003eTerminalBench Fiz-Wrapper Comparison\u003c/ref\u003e\n  \u003c/governing\u003e\n\u003c/execute-bead\u003e\n","metadata":{"attempt_id":"20260507T030529-d3ec7c21","base_rev":"c74ff88355fb252cb99538af919baf671bc82465","bead_id":"fizeau-9ff62c35","bundle_path":".ddx/executions/20260507T030529-d3ec7c21","correlation_id":"fizeau-9ff62c35:20260507T030529-d3ec7c21","prompt_file":".ddx/executions/20260507T030529-d3ec7c21/prompt.md","prompt_sha":"5a4e90b482e784125adda1b74b7259dd08f94596384e04695989835981e3ae76","role":"implementer","session_id":"eb-7e93bf8b","worker_id":""}}}
